  "note": "Total Assets = Total Liabilities + Equity reconciles exactly. Interest income minus interest paid = net interest income exactly; PBT minus tax = net profit exactly. DISCREPANCY FOUND: the bank's own 2019 Q1 report's Jan'18-Mar'18 comparative column shows 'Other operating income' as 26,737,029 (vs 29,552,422 contemporaneously reported here) and 'Provision against loans and advances' as 37,184,607 (vs 40,000,000 contemporaneously reported here) — both off by exactly 2,815,393 BDT in opposite directions, netting to zero effect on Profit before provision through net profit (PBT, tax and net profit after tax are identical, 141,986,446/123,049,754/18,936,692, in both reports). This looks like a minor reclassification between an income line and a provision line, not a profit restatement. Contemporaneous line-item values (29,552,422 / 40,000,000) are kept per project convention."
